## Explanation of Each Directive Block

### 1. `limit_req_zone` (Top-Level)
```nginx
limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=api_limit:10m rate=20r/s;
```
- **`$binary_remote_addr`**: Uses the binary representation of the client IP for memory efficiency.
- **`zone=api_limit:10m`**: Creates a shared memory zone named `api_limit` with 10MB capacity (supports ~160,000 unique IPs).
- **`rate=20r/s`**: Sets the rate limit to 20 requests per second per IP.

### 2. `upstream api_backend`
```nginx
upstream api_backend {
    server 127.0.0.1:8080;
    keepalive 32;
}
```
- **`server 127.0.0.1:8080`**: Defines the backend API server.
- **`keepalive 32`**: Maintains up to 32 idle keepalive connections to the backend, reducing TCP handshake overhead for subsequent requests.

### 3. HTTP Server Block (Port 80)
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name _;
    return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
}
```
- **`listen 80` / `listen [::]:80`**: Listens on IPv4 and IPv6 port 80.
- **`server_name _`**: Catches all hostnames (default server).
- **`return 301 https://$host$request_uri`**: Permanently redirects all HTTP traffic to HTTPS, preserving the original host and URI.

### 4. TLS Configuration (Inside HTTPS Server)
```nginx
ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/ssl/api.crt;
ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/ssl/api.key;
ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
ssl_ciphers ECDHE-ECDSA-AES128-GCM-SHA256:...;
ssl_prefer_server_ciphers on;
ssl_session_cache shared:SSL:10m;
ssl_session_timeout 1d;
ssl_session_tickets off;
ssl_stapling on;
ssl_stapling_verify on;
resolver 8.8.8.8 8.8.4.4 valid=300s;
resolver_timeout 5s;
```
- **`ssl_certificate` / `ssl_certificate_key`**: Paths to the TLS certificate and private key.
- **`ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3`**: Only allows modern TLS versions, disabling insecure older protocols.
- **`ssl_ciphers`**: Specifies a strong cipher suite prioritizing ECDHE key exchange, AES-GCM/ChaCha20 encryption, and SHA-256/38

